In your browser ["Your email address, the times you sign in, and a record of each sign-in. Supabase Auth, our sign-in service, keeps these. Its records include your IP address and your browser's description of itself.","Your date of birth, if you are old enough to continue. We keep it in our database with an account ID and the time the record was made.","The words you type into the home screen's question box and any file you attach stay in your browser. They are not sent or stored. The app does not use your microphone.","PLANNED","Your name, interests, level, goal, and choice of tutor voice, which setup will ask for.","Each lesson's title, subject, language, length, transcript, and board drawings, kept while the account is active.","Your browser keeps your sign-in and your light or dark choice in local storage. Its session storage holds the email address you last asked a sign-in link for and the time you asked.","When an account closes, or a closed account signs in again, the app sets one cookie that stops new sign-ups on this browser for a day. It holds no name, address, or date, it expires by itself, and nothing on our servers reads it. Accounts already set up can still sign in. The app sets no other cookies and runs no analytics or advertising code."]
